+// ── G-LIVE-21 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+//
+// FORCED COLOURS, THE DECK. There the drawn ring is `display: none` and the UA outline is the
+// indicator; the deck keeps DOM focus on its scrollport (an `aria-activedescendant` listbox), and
+// the scrollport draws no ring of its own on purpose. So the ACTIVE CARD must carry the outline,
+// or a High Contrast reader has nothing at all on the deck (measured on this tree before the cure:
+// card `none`, scrollport `none`, ring hidden — both engines). Chromium applies the emulation;
+// the row reads `matchMedia` rather than trusting it.
+test("G-LIVE-21 · forced colours: the deck's active card carries the outline", async ({
