+// invite path — a dist never forms a room). A peer writes; the phone TAPS that cell; the tape
+// rises naming the author. Two invariants, each with its reading and its negative control:
+//   · the tape TAKES NO TAP — `elementFromPoint` at the label's own centre is not the tape, and a
+//     negative control in the same run (the tape made hit-testable) proves the read can see it;
+//   · the tape and YOUR ring never share a pixel on your own cell (air ≥ 0 px).
+// What it does NOT bound, and says so: how many OTHER cells the tape lies over. That count is
+// the slug's length (6 cells at 85.63 px, 10 at 131.63 px, pass 3/4) and W2 §2.5's covering law
+// reads it RED at `74a2b5d9` too — the chair's booked row (pass5/CHAIR-RULINGS §1.4, the T9-R5
+// candidate), and a bounded tape is the owner's Arm B. The count rides as an annotation.
+test("G-LIVE-17 · the coarse tape names a cell and takes no tap (room, 390×844 coarse)", async ({
